<title>SPAIN: Spain's BCH group Q1 attributable 12.45 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>Spain's BCH group Q1 attributable 12.45 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Central Hispano group, three months to March results (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit	     12.45    vs    10.37</p>
<p> Net interest income		   71.21    vs    63.74</p>
<p> Profit on equity portfolio	   2.36    vs     2.87</p>
<p> Financial margin			73.58    vs    66.61</p>
<p> Ordinary margin			102.39    vs    93.03</p>
<p> Operating income			32.40    vs    24.58</p>
<p> Operating costs			 69.97    vs    68.46</p>
<p> Extraordinary losses		  (3.74)   vs    (2.77)</p>
<p> Insolvency provisions		 21.16    vs    22.57</p>
<p> Net provisions			   8.44    vs     7.42</p>
<p> Pretax profit			   19.84    vs    14.01</p>
<p> Net profit				16.86    vs    12.40</p>
<p> Minorities				 4.41    vs     2.03</p>
<p>NOTE: BCH said return on equity stood at 12.5 percent versus 10.6 percent.</p>
</text>
